1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,810
Slide 33 outlines "DESIGNING THE DIGITAL MANDATE: The Three Boundary Invariants."

2
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:13,523
Every Digital Mandate consists of three non-negotiable walls: Card 1: Scope Invariants.

3
00:00:13,523 --> 00:00:17,866
The agent is restricted strictly to whitelisted domain endpoints.

4
00:00:17,866 --> 00:00:22,210
It cannot communicate with unauthorized darkweb or proxy servers!

5
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:25,119
Card 2: Financial Ceilings.

6
00:00:25,119 --> 00:00:33,380
Unalterable programmatic budget caps enforced locally in C++ or Python before the network packet is even built!

7
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:36,328
And Card 3: Temporal Bounds!

8
00:00:36,328 --> 00:00:40,937
Every authorization credential self-destructs after 60 minutes.

9
00:00:40,937 --> 00:00:46,500
If a task stalls or network times out, the authorization expires harmlessly!

10
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:54,100
Scope, Budget, and Time: if any of the three boundaries are violated, the mandate drops dead instantly!

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,440
Strict mathematical boundaries transform probabilistic neural networks into reliable enterprise infrastructure.

